  "delivered_messages_sha256": "e0170cd343b59b1a1905f11f5547cab9d41bf176e57682407b752d457e345849",
  "raw_text": "Yes. `git reset --hard` discards uncommitted changes to **tracked files** in both the working tree and staging area, resetting them to the target commit.\n\n```bash\ngit reset --hard HEAD\n```\n\nThis usually cannot be undone through Git if the edits were never committed or stashed.\n\nIt does **not** remove untracked files. To remove those, use `git clean`—carefully:\n\n```bash\ngit clean -nfd  # preview\ngit clean -fd   # delete untracked files/directories\n```",
